commit 463c9a133a6dfea9adf1e6c8e07ab705cbf2a587
Author:     Dongkyun Son <dongkyun.s@samsung.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Nov 2 22:22:34 2026 +0900
Commit:     Dongkyun Son <dongkyun.s@samsung.com>
CommitDate: Tue Nov 3 15:59:19 2026 +0900

    packaging: classify -feliminate-unused-debug-types and mirror recorded backend policy
    
    The x86_64 native-archive-conversion step rejects unknown tokens recorded in
    the IR llvm.commandline metadata. Tizen's default CFLAGS inject
    -feliminate-unused-debug-types and --param, which the classifier did not
    know. Also, profiles without -gdwarf-4 or -ffunction-sections in CFLAGS
    (release builds strip them) failed the certified sanity checks even after
    classification.
    
    - classify -feliminate-unused-debug-types as frontend semantics (debug-type
      emission is already materialized in the input IR)
    - consume --param / --param= as driver tuning operands
    - derive the replay backend policy from the recorded command instead of a
      fixed flag set: -f/-fno- per section switch, and -g -gdwarf-4 only when
      the original command recorded debug options
    - keep unique-section-names/addrsig certification and the -gdwarf-4
      requirement when debug options are present (fail-closed)
    
    Toolchain-profile replay flags are byte-identical to the previous policy;
    Dev-profile (no debug, no section flags) now replays faithfully.
    
    Fixes QuickBuild 1214821 (x86_64 %install failure:
    ValueError: unclassified original command token: -feliminate-unused-debug-types).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Cline SR
    Change-Id: I1c0d0bcccb1dc3c64efbb635e3e6f3de6748209e

